Bootstrap: docker
From: condaforge/miniforge3:24.3.0-0

%labels
    Maintainer sdweave2@ncsu.edu
    Source https://github.com/metaGmetapop/metapop
    Version 0.0.60

%help
    MetaPop — a pipeline for the macro- and micro-diversity analyses and
    visualization of metagenomic-derived populations.

    MetaPop processes short-read data mapped to reference genomes to
    calculate sample-level diversity metrics (abundance, population
    diversity, similarity) and within-species diversity (nucleotide
    polymorphisms and amino acid substitutions), with graphical summaries
    of the results. It is organized into four modules: Preprocessing,
    Microdiversity, Macrodiversity, and Visualization.

    Installed from PyPI (metapop 0.0.60), which provides the `metapop`
    entry point documented upstream. Note: the bioconda "metapop" package
    is NOT this tool's Python pipeline — it is built from jiarong/MetaPop
    and ships only the older standalone MetaPop.R scripts.

    Usage:
        apptainer run metapop-0.0.60.sif --input_samples <BAM dir> \
            --reference <reference genome(s)> --norm <read counts file> [OPTIONS]

    Run `apptainer run metapop-0.0.60.sif --help` for the full option list.

%post -c /bin/bash
    set -e

    # Hazel bind-mount points
    mkdir -p /rs1 /share /home /usr/local/usrapps

    # Runtime deps exactly as listed in upstream's README install steps
    # (miniforge3 + mamba per CLAUDE.md lesson 2), then the PyPI package.
    mamba create -n metapop -y -c conda-forge -c bioconda \
        python=3.10 pip numpy pysam samtools bcftools prodigal \
        r-base r-data.table r-ggplot2 r-ggrepel r-rcolorbrewer r-doparallel \
        r-cowplot r-bit64 r-gggenes r-stringr r-vegan r-compositions r-pheatmap
    /opt/conda/envs/metapop/bin/pip install --no-cache-dir metapop==0.0.60
    mamba clean -afy

%environment
    export PATH=/opt/conda/envs/metapop/bin:$PATH

%runscript
    exec metapop "$@"

%test
    metapop --help
